---
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageMeta from '@/components/PageMeta.astro';
import GatewayCard from '@/components/ia/GatewayCard.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="PDTF schema"
  description="A third-party input to SPDTF: the existing Digital Property Pack schema, its supporting material and a separately status-labelled ontology derived from it."
>
  <PageMeta category="SPDTF · third-party input" variant="info" updated="PDTF schema package v3.5.0 · supporting and derived artefacts vary in status" />
  <h1>PDTF schema</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    The PDTF schema is a third-party input to SPDTF: the existing Digital Property Pack JSON Schema package. Its data
    dictionary, business glossary, overlays and implementation material explain that
    schema-led exchange contract. A separate draft ontology was later derived from those
    sources and is retained as evidence for SPDTF.
  </p>

  <div class="callout callout--key">
    <p class="callout__label">Read the status carefully</p>
    <p>
      The PDTF schema was not an OPDA-endorsed scheme. Its technical publication does not
      confer scheme authority, and it does not grant inherited authority to supporting or
      derived artefacts. Each ontology, model, mapping, pilot and implementation record
      retains the status shown on its own page.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="contents">Third-party source material and derived evidence</h2>
  <div class="card-grid">
    <GatewayCard href="/spdtf/inputs/pdtf-schema/schema-and-supporting-material" title="Schema and supporting material" eyebrow="Third-party source" description="JSON Schemas and overlays, data dictionary, business glossary, implementation guidance and attributed usage evidence." />
    <GatewayCard href="/spdtf/inputs/pdtf-schema/schema-derived-ontology" title="Schema-derived ontology" eyebrow="Separate draft artefact" description="The ontology derived from schema-led sources, with model views, qualified mappings, provenance and known limitations." />
  </div>

  <p>
    Implementers can go directly to the <a href="/spdtf/inputs/pdtf-schema/schema-and-supporting-material/schema">Schemas and overlays</a> or
    <a href="/spdtf/inputs/pdtf-schema/schema-and-supporting-material/implementation">Implementation guidance</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="continuation">From schema to scheme</h2>
  <p>
    Existing dictionaries, glossary entries, documentation, schemas and mappings are
    attributed inputs to the first collaboratively authored SPDTF scheme draft. The PDTF
    schema can inform compatibility, constraints, coverage and migration; the
    schema-derived ontology can inform semantic review. Neither source determines new
    domain identities or relationships merely because it encoded them previously.
  </p>
  <p>
    <a href="/spdtf">Read the SPDTF development method</a> or
    <a href="/semantic-modelling/evidence-and-mappings">trace how evidence and mappings are qualified</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="identifiers">Route and identifier boundary</h2>
  <p>
    Reader documentation now follows the <code>/spdtf/inputs/pdtf-schema/**</code> hierarchy. Earlier
    documentation routes are removed without redirects. The separate <code>/pdtf/**</code>
    RDF identifier namespace remains unchanged because those values identify resources in
    the schema-derived ontology rather than pages in the reader hierarchy.
  </p>
</Layout>
